ID: vr-20
Title: Preserve Claire and add extensible performance-first presentation views
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/19

Status: DONE
Milestone: Claire, FaceMesh, FaceDot and UniformPolygons share one speaking face.
Dependencies: vr-13, vr-14, vr-15

Purpose:
The owner likes the present Claire lip motion/expressions and wants it preserved,
with performance prioritized. Add three selectable presentations now, without
changing the learned model. The future supplied GLB is named Realistic but
vr-16..19 remain parked; naming it does not resume asset adaptation.

Tasks:
[x] 20.1 Preserve Claire as the fresh-load default, including its material,
    hair/edge/point settings, full-bust option and unchanged speech pipeline.
[x] 20.2 Add a small explicit presentation registry and reversible selection.
    No audio replacement, regeneration, seeking or extra rendering loop.
[x] 20.3 Implement FaceMesh as a front-face-only triangular wire mask, without
    ears, neck or hair. Add bounded detail levels, native detail by default,
    actual reduced index work and protected lip/eye/nose regions.
    Reject incompatible adjacency and incident rest-triangle winding changes.
[x] 20.4 Implement FaceDot as visible surface dots, including ears/eyes/neck.
    Use a hidden depth surface for occlusion, never a visible filled skin/line
    pass; suppress hair without altering Claire's saved choices.
[x] 20.5 Implement UniformPolygons as a surface-anchored rectangular grid.
    Disclose curved/deformed cells and the underlying triangle depth surface;
    do not claim new quad retopology or perfectly rectangular curved anatomy.
[x] 20.6 Preserve gaze, XYZ, framing where applicable, one desktop overlay,
    RAM-only speech, capability routing and explicit graphics/setup failures.
    Bound topology/cache resources and skip unused shaded-normal updates.
[x] 20.7 Add focused geometry/switching tests; qualify actual browser/native
    pixels, motion, density, alpha, reset/restart and comparable performance.
    Keep failures, actual raster density and human-acceptance limits.
[x] 20.8 Update guide/README/book/index/ledger and issue/Project evidence;
    publish only the coherent verified source milestone, not a new release.

Acceptance criteria:
Claire round-trips exactly with its prior choices and stays the initial view.
All three named views display actual animated Claire geometry, not image
overlays or an unrelated model. FaceMesh removes non-face geometry and reduces
submitted primitives at lower detail without welding opposite lips/eyelids.
FaceDot shows no colored polygons/lines and occludes hidden points. Uniform
grid follows the surface under speech/rotation instead of a screen-space grid.
Changing view/detail preserves the current audio source/time and expression.
View resources stay bounded; unlit modes do not compute unused animated normals.
Existing local/privacy/lifecycle behavior remains, with no automatic install,
asset download, Realistic integration, device activation or sibling interaction.
Performance is measured, not inferred solely from polygon counts.

